                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jeremy Kerr",
                        "email": "jk@ozlabs.org",
                        "username": "jk-ozlabs"
                    },
                    "message": "Ack: we'll need to have the custom definitions available as meson setup time, so the only sensible approach here is with options\n\n(unless the sizes header can consume compile-time values, but that sounds like a bit of a maintenance nightmare)"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Johnston",
                        "email": "matt@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "mkj"
                    },
                    "message": "Yeah, meson compiler tests (like sizeof) explicitly don't use any provided arguments so that wouldn't work.\n\n> These compiler checks do not use compiler arguments added with add_*_arguments(), via -Dlang_args on the command-line, or through CFLAGS/LDFLAGS, etc in the environment. Hence, you can trust that the tests will be fully self-contained, and won't fail because of custom flags added by other parts of the build file or by users."
                }
            ],
